# Shell scripts must reach the guest with LF endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this checkout, and a corpus case checked out with
# CRLF fails INSIDE tobyOS in a way that looks like a shell bug: the guest's
# bash sees the stray CR and exits 2 with a syntax error, while MSYS bash on
# the host tolerates it and reports the same file as fine. That cost a full
# build-and-boot cycle to track down once already.
*.sh text eol=lf
